      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those platitudes can feel completely hollow when you are experiencing such deep, existential darkness. What you are describing is profound grief—the loss of your narrative and your related life meaning. It is valid to feel meaningless when your foundation has been removed. Please consider that while your *old* meaning is gone, you have the radical, terrifying freedom to begin building a new sense of purpose entirely from within yourself. If the darkness feels absolute, finding a safe space to talk to someone who understands emotional depth could help you find a flicker of light.",
      "source": "target",
